        "id": 1021605
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-14T20:27:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "VP8 does not use a formal profile and level system (such as the ones found in H.264 or VP9). Instead, the VP8 specification defines a single unified feature baseline with simple bitstream versions.\n\nSince version 0 bitstream support is required for all decoders, the additional versions are more akin to the concept of \"reduced encoding complexity\". As such in Codec 2.0 we specifically not define a profile or a level, and invite encoder implementations to implement support for the various levels via the complexity parameter.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 750,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 750,
        "endChar": 23
      },
      "revId": "8571d7700b363788db3a7bcf117949fddfc3cd3f",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
